      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your honesty touches on the very \"absurd\" that Albert Camus and others have debated for over a century. Instead of \"finding weight\" in a meaningless cosmos, the solution is to accept that the \"nothing\" you fear is the final act, while the \"doing\" you feel is the entire play. We stop trying to \"justify\" the struggle and stop \"worrying\" about the end, which is a act of defiance in itself.\n\n**\n.\n.\n.",
